CHECK:LINE_SPACING: Please use a blank line after function/struct/union/enum declarations
#67: FILE: drivers/acpi/iort.c:38:
+};
+static LIST_HEAD(iort_fwnode_list);

Vertical space is wasted given the limited number of lines an
editor window can display when multiple blank lines are used.

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#spaces

CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kzalloc(sizeof(*np)...) over kzalloc(sizeof(struct iort_fwnode)...)
#85: FILE: drivers/acpi/iort.c:56:
+	np = kzalloc(sizeof(struct iort_fwnode), GFP_KERNEL);

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

WARNING:BLOCK_COMMENT_STYLE: Block comments should align the * on each line
#107: FILE: drivers/acpi/iort.c:78:
+ * Returns: fwnode_handle pointer on success NULL on failure
+*/

The comment style is incorrect.  The preferred style for multi-
line comments is::

  /*
  * This is the preferred style
  * for multi line comments.
  */

The networking comment style is a bit different, with the first line
not empty like the former::

  /* This is the preferred comment style
  * for files in net/ and drivers/net/
  */

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#commenting

